abstract="The parser realizes the syntactic analysis of programs. Its input is a sequence of 
  symbols as produced by the combination of scanner and screener. The parser is meant to identify 
  the syntactic structure in this sequence of symbols, that is how the syntactic units are composed 
  from other units. Syntactic units in imperative languages are, for example, variables, expressions, 
  declarations, statements, and sequences of statements.",
